<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27028" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lūbrĭco</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		lubricus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make smooth</i> or <i>slippery, to
				lubricate</i> (postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui Lacedaemonium pytismate lubricat orbem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 175</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lubricatus lapis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 1, 22</span></i>
			; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 11,
			38.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To be slippery</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Thren. 4, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">limo caenoso ripae supercilio lubricante,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, 18</span></i>
			 (p. 481), 196, 3.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lubricatus,</span>”
				<i>anointed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 571</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
